---
import Layout from '../layouts/doc.astro';
import { TokenTable } from '../components/token-table';
import themeTokensData from '../data/theme-tokens.json';

const solace: Record<string, string> = themeTokensData.solace;

/** Look up a token's resolved value in the Solace palette (docs default). */
function val(name: string): string {
  return solace[name] ?? "";
}

const backgrounds = [
  { name: "--color-bg", usage: "Page background" },
  { name: "--color-bg-raised", usage: "Cards, panels" },
  { name: "--color-bg-overlay", usage: "Dialogs, menus, popovers" },
  { name: "--color-bg-input", usage: "Form controls" },
  { name: "--color-bg-hover", usage: "Hover surface" },
  { name: "--color-bg-active", usage: "Active / selected surface" },
  { name: "--color-bg-disabled", usage: "Disabled surface" },
  { name: "--color-bg-emphasis", usage: "Primary buttons, checked, tooltips, pagination current" },
  { name: "--color-bg-emphasis-hover", usage: "Emphasis surface, hovered (accent-warmed)" },
  { name: "--color-bg-emphasis-active", usage: "Emphasis surface, pressed (accent-warmed)" },
].map(t => ({ ...t, value: val(t.name) }));

const foregrounds = [
  { name: "--color-fg", usage: "Primary text" },
  { name: "--color-fg-muted", usage: "Secondary text, descriptions" },
  { name: "--color-fg-subtle", usage: "Placeholders, decorative text" },
  { name: "--color-fg-disabled", usage: "Disabled text" },
  { name: "--color-fg-on-emphasis", usage: "Text on bg-emphasis" },
  { name: "--color-fg-link", usage: "Links" },
].map(t => ({ ...t, value: val(t.name) }));

const borders = [
  { name: "--color-border", usage: "Default borders" },
  { name: "--color-border-muted", usage: "Dividers, disabled borders" },
  { name: "--color-border-strong", usage: "Inputs, overlays, emphasis" },
  { name: "--color-border-focus", usage: "Focus outline" },
].map(t => ({ ...t, value: val(t.name) }));

const roleSlots = [
  { name: "--color-{role}-solid", key: "--color-danger-solid", usage: "Solid fill (buttons, badges)" },
  { name: "--color-{role}-fg-on-solid", key: "--color-danger-fg-on-solid", usage: "Type on the solid — the knockout" },
  { name: "--color-{role}-solid-hover", key: "--color-danger-solid-hover", usage: "Solid, hovered" },
  { name: "--color-{role}-solid-active", key: "--color-danger-solid-active", usage: "Solid, pressed" },
  { name: "--color-{role}-fg", key: "--color-danger-fg", usage: "Role-colored text on the page" },
  { name: "--color-{role}-bg", key: "--color-danger-bg", usage: "Tinted background" },
  { name: "--color-{role}-border", key: "--color-danger-border", usage: "Border on tinted background" },
  { name: "--color-accent-bg-subtle", key: "--color-accent-bg-subtle", usage: "Accent only — faintest wash (the lens fill — navigation, tabs)" },
].map(t => ({ name: t.name, usage: t.usage, value: val(t.key) }));

const shadows = [
  { name: "--shadow-offset", usage: "Surfaces (cards, panels)" },
  { name: "--shadow-offset-overlay", usage: "Overlays" },
  { name: "--shadow-offset-action", usage: "Thin action edge — pressable hover or field focus" },
  { name: "--shadow-offset-action-hover", usage: "Grown action edge — open owner" },
  { name: "--shadow-offset-action-danger", usage: "Invalid writing field, focused" },
].map(t => ({ ...t, value: val(t.name) }));

const palette = [
  { name: "--surface-0 … --surface-2", key: "--surface-0", usage: "The page and what sits on it" },
  { name: "--tone-0 … --tone-7, --tone-11", key: "--tone-7", usage: "Functional neutral ramp: paper through deepest ink" },
  { name: "--tone-8 … --tone-10", key: "--tone-9", usage: "Reserved: 12-step ramp compatibility and future deep-ink roles" },
  { name: "--signal-{role}", key: "--signal-danger", usage: "One ink per meaning; only the accent is vivid" },
  { name: "--signal-{role}-on", key: "--signal-danger-on", usage: "Which ramp end carries type on each solid" },
  { name: "--shadow-size / -color / -color-overlay", key: "--shadow-color", usage: "Shadow geometry and ink" },
].map(t => ({ name: t.name, usage: t.usage, value: val(t.key) }));
---

<Layout title="Design Tokens">

<h1>Design Tokens</h1>

<p>Three layers. The theme-independent foundation supplies type, spacing, borders, and radii. A theme authors <strong>30 palette values</strong>; 27 feed the <strong>68 semantic names</strong> components actually use, while <code>--tone-8</code> through <code>--tone-10</code> are reserved to preserve the public 12-step neutral ramp and support future deep-ink roles. The <code>init</code> command adds all three layers to your CSS file — after that you own them. Values shown are Solace (default). See <a href="/ui/themes">Themes</a> for other presets.</p>

<h2>Background</h2>

<TokenTable tokens={backgrounds} />

<p>Use as Tailwind utilities: <code>bg-bg</code>, <code>bg-bg-raised</code>, <code>bg-bg-emphasis</code>, etc.</p>

<h2>Foreground</h2>

<TokenTable tokens={foregrounds} />

<p>Use as <code>text-fg</code>, <code>text-fg-muted</code>, <code>text-fg-link</code>, etc.</p>

<h2>Border</h2>

<TokenTable tokens={borders} />

<p>Use as <code>border-border</code>, <code>divide-border-muted</code>, <code>outline-border-focus</code>, etc.</p>

<h2>Contrast guarantees</h2>

<p>Beaket tests supported semantic combinations in Chromium after CSS variables and <code>color-mix()</code> expressions resolve. Normal-sized primary, muted, subtle, link, emphasis, and role text combinations meet at least <strong>4.5:1</strong>. Default, strong, focus, and invalid interactive boundaries meet at least <strong>3:1</strong> against their supported surfaces.</p>

<p>These are guarantees for the documented semantic pairings, not an all-against-all promise. Decorative surfaces are intentionally excluded. Disabled text and boundaries are measured and reported to theme authors, but they are not presented as WCAG failures because inactive controls are exempt from the corresponding WCAG contrast requirements. Run <code>pnpm test:contrast</code> from the repository root to audit every shipped light and dark palette.</p>

<h2>Solace signal distinguishability</h2>

<p>Solace additionally tests every pair of its six semantic roles as a solid, foreground, tint, 1px border, hover, and active color under normal vision and simulated protanopia, deuteranopia, and tritanopia. The simulation applies the 100% severity matrices from <a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/TVCG.2009.113">Machado, Oliveira, and Fernandes (2009)</a> to linear-light sRGB. Distances are then measured as Euclidean ΔE in OKLab.</p>

<p>The undiluted solid, hover, and active forms require ΔE ≥ <strong>0.04</strong>. Derived forms scale that floor by the semantic layer's authored OKLab mixture: foreground 50% requires <strong>0.02</strong>, tint 17% requires <strong>0.007</strong>, and border 60% requires <strong>0.025</strong> (rounded up). The base floor is a Beaket safety margin for small marks, not a WCAG rule or a universal perception boundary. Tints remain supporting surfaces; shipped status examples retain readable labels or distinct icon shapes so color is never the only cue.</p>

<h2>Roles</h2>

<p>Six roles — <code>danger</code>, <code>success</code>, <code>warning</code>, <code>info</code>, <code>info-alt</code>, <code>accent</code> — each with seven slots. Values below show the <code>danger</code> role. The accent role alone carries one extra slot, <code>-bg-subtle</code>.</p>

<TokenTable tokens={roleSlots} />

<p>Use as <code>bg-danger-solid</code>, <code>text-danger-fg-on-solid</code>, <code>text-success-fg</code>, <code>bg-info-bg</code>, <code>border-warning-border</code>, etc.</p>

<h2>Shadows</h2>

<TokenTable tokens={shadows} showSwatch={false} />

<p>Surfaces use <code>shadow-offset</code>; overlays use <code>shadow-offset-overlay</code>. Pressables are neutral at rest: edged controls reveal <code>shadow-offset-action</code> on hover, and open owners hold <code>shadow-offset-action-hover</code>. Writing fields engage the thin edge only on focus, swapping to <code>shadow-offset-action-danger</code> when invalid. Size and color vary by theme.</p>

<h2>Palette — authored by the theme</h2>

<p>The layer a theme supplies. Components never reference these directly; the semantic names above point at them.</p>

<TokenTable tokens={palette} showSwatch={false} />

<h2>Customization</h2>

<p>After <code>init</code>, these tokens are yours. To restyle an app, edit the 30 palette values — the semantic layer follows. The library will not update them automatically. Check the <a href="/ui/changelog">Changelog</a> when updating.</p>

</Layout>
